# Embedded Sensor Testing Simulator

## Overview

A Python-based software simulator for testing sensor data from an embedded/IoT device.

The project demonstrates functional testing, boundary testing, negative testing, missing-data validation, invalid-data handling, and automated test-result generation.

## Objectives

- Simulate embedded sensor readings
- Validate temperature and humidity values
- Validate accelerometer readings
- Test boundary conditions
- Test invalid sensor values
- Test missing sensor data
- Generate automated PASS/FAIL results
- Export test results to CSV

## Sensors Simulated

- Temperature
- Humidity
- Accelerometer X
- Accelerometer Y
- Accelerometer Z

## Testing Types

### Functional Testing

Verifies that valid sensor readings are accepted.

### Boundary Testing

Checks sensor values at defined limits.

### Negative Testing

Checks how the system handles invalid or out-of-range values.

### Missing Data Testing

Checks the behavior when sensor data is unavailable.

### Invalid Data Testing

Checks the behavior when non-numeric sensor data is received.

## Technologies

- Python
- CSV
- Embedded/IoT testing concepts
- Sensor data validation
